# The unserved shares of a layer, totalled, with what would suspend the total. One row per layer
# holding at least one `customer` or `unrealised` share: how many such holders, how many left
# their share unstated, the sum of the ones that stated it, and the units they used.
#
# One population for both callers
#   arithmetic/exposure_bounded.sqlc inner-joins entries/unserved_holders.sqlc, so a layer with no
#   unserved holder is not a candidate. checks/exposure_unaccounted.sqlc needs the same γ. Computed
#   separately with an outer join and `coalesce(unserved, 0)`, layers with no unserved holder enter
#   the check's examined set carrying a zero nobody filed; they read `exposure = 0`, so the check
#   cannot fire on any of them and still counts them toward its coverage, examining more than the
#   site declares.
#
# An unstated share is not a zero share
#   That is why `unstated` is a column and not a filter. `sum()` skips NULLs silently, so a layer
#   where nobody stated a share sums to NULL and one where half did sums to half the truth. Both
#   callers must decide what to do about that, and they decide differently: the site reports
#   `suspended`, the check declines to examine. Carrying the count lets each say so instead of each
#   rediscovering it. `derived` counts the unstated shares filed as `sharesSum`'s output, as in
#   entries/holder_totals.sqlc, so a caller can name the identity it waits on.
#
# `share_units` is the distinct set
#   A caller comparing against its layer's own unit asks whether that set is exactly its own unit
#   and nothing else. A NULL unit lands in the array and makes the comparison false, which is
#   correct: an unstated unit is not a matching one.
-- entries/unserved_holders.sqlc folded to one row per layer.
SELECT h.filing, h.layer,
       count(*)                                        AS holders,
       count(*) FILTER (WHERE h.share_high IS NULL)     AS unstated,
       count(*) FILTER (WHERE h.share_derivation IS NOT NULL) AS derived,
       sum(h.share_high)                                AS unserved_high,
       sum(h.share_mode)                                AS unserved_mode,
       array_agg(DISTINCT h.share_unit)                 AS share_units
FROM (
    :compose(entries/unserved_holders.sqlc)
) h
GROUP BY h.filing, h.layer
